{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1215237-iteration-x-procedures","id":1215237,"title":"Iteration X procedures","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-04T14:41:13-07:00","id":1215237,"title":"Iteration X procedures","content":"Hello all!<br /> <br /> So I finally got a chance to finally take a look at ItX's revised Splatbook and loved the heck out of it. In the past I always had trouble enjoying a faction that kinda represented everything I hated, especially through this idea of turning its new members into cogs in the machine both literally and figuratively. However, quotes like this form the new book make ItX more like a group of like minded scientists/ engineers who are trying to master the world and improve themselves in a more relatable way<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Iteration X, as a Convention, tries to make that understanding innate. These Technocrats attempt to encompass that degree of knowledge and bring it into their personal lives to varying degrees. Some focus on the extension of the worldmachine into the Self, and become cyborgs and the augmented, extending the abilities of those most natural of tools, their bodies. Some attempt to push the Self outward into the world-machine, to upload their very personalities into artificial intelligences, to create new methods of personnel management that lets the group Self become its own tool. Some are more removed, exploring the space of the world-machine, attempting to divine its laws and rules and to make of the whole a tool for their ends, and to that purpose they create new materials, they surround the Self in literal oceans of data, they design devices of startling complexity to allow the Self to find the limits of what can be accomplished and, having seen them, move beyond. </div> </div> </div>. <br /> <br /> I really like this take a lot and I came to quickly see that going cyborg is both accepted but not as enforced or pursued anymore within the rankings of ItX <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are guys like that out there, but they\u2019re 20 years past their culture and they know it. Most of them are hardcore old-time Biomechanics who\u2019ve been leaning toward the Cult of the Machine because it gives their egos a tweak. The rest of we slightly-more-well-adjusted-geek types pretty much feel that as long as you\u2019re happy with the way you are, its all good to us and we don\u2019t care much. </div> </div> </div><b>The point of all of this is to ask, what kind of magic does ItX do and what does it look like?</b>. Every single Convention got a set of procedures in their revised edition, but oddly there are none present in ItX, just a ton of hardsuits and wonders. As much as I love to see cool devices I wanted to know what a ItX member can be expected to do if he isn't some completely decked out cyborg like they have always been in the past (such as if he was a macrotechnician). What would a Iteration X member do in a fight if they do not have any cyborg enhancements at all? Can I expect them to use the worlds tools to craft themselves a jury rigged device, or to employ enlightened statistics to tactically outsmart their enemy? Would I see them cooking up some explosives to fight off an enemy or is none of this possible within their paradigm? Do ItX always need to create wonders in a lab to do their magic or can they actually be more free form?<br /> <br /> What does this idea of the world being your tool come to in terms of being an Iteration X mage?<br /> <br /> ||Let me know what you think||<br /> <br /> -Brassfist<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16848-brassfist","name":"Brassfist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T17:09:10-07:00","id":1215274,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine it would be a lot like Etherites and Virtual Adepts, just more conventional in design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T18:37:36-07:00","id":1215304,"title":"","content":"A lot of the time, their effects at least in some of the books I've read, are very perception focused. Targeting Computations, a Correspondence/Forces effect that allows you to treat all ranges within the actual physical range of the weapon as point blank range, as well as allowing you to ignore cover that is not hard cover, is a good example. It doesn't call down lightning or fire. It's not even useful without a gun.<br /> <br /> But with a gun? It makes the Iterator TERRIFYING. And IIRC Much of their effects fall along these lines. There are a few vulgar physical effects, but for the most part it's all effects that would fall under the trope &quot;awesomeness by analysis&quot; When designing an effect for an iterator, take two things into mind.<br /> <br /> 1.) Iteration X hates failure. They prefer to prepare prepare prepare, and then do it perfectly the first time rather than attempt something half-prepared and hope for the best.<br /> 2.) Information is king. The more you know, the more control you have. The better your ability to predict reality, the closer you are to ascension.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T21:38:58-07:00","id":1215348,"title":"","content":"Iteration X's first edition book had several rotes, er procedures. Time Motion Managers do a lot of statistical and predictive work, so they can do nasty things with Entropy to determine probable actions. They may not call it Dim Mak, but you can bet any Iterator with Entropy 1 will know where to maximize their damage.<br /> <br /> Iteration X is also very good with Matter, so expect them to have really good gear and be able to improvise in a non-cinematic way.<br /> <br /> If you have the Book of Mirrors, the Mage storyteller's guide from Mage 1e/2e, there's a list of all the rotes by book up to its publication date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T01:36:48-07:00","id":1215405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brassfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1215237-iteration-x-procedures#post1215237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Would I see them cooking up some explosives to fight off an enemy or is none of this possible within their paradigm? Do ItX always need to create wonders in a lab to do their magic or can they actually be more free form?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As per the material written on the Technocracy and the Iteration-X Convention, they would need to prepare their Procedures in a machine shop or a laboratory beforehand. Building machines and devices, tuning machines and devices, recharging power, adjusting settings etc. Any tools and measurement devices would be created or modified in a laboratory or a machine shop beforehand. I think that this is within the Convention's Paradigm - their Inspired Science is so far ahead of what is most of the time possible in the world, that they cannot do their Effects without first doing all of their technocratic preparations and having the needed, specified tools and materials.<br /> <br /> I recall the revised Iteration-X Convention Book talking a lot about how the Iteration-X uses tools to accomplish their Magick - as per this, I think that free-form improvisation is discouraged, in favour of creating and preparing the right tools - machines, materials, devices - beforehand to be able to do a given Magickal Effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is a small amount of writings ( a Procedure here and there , and not much else that I know of ) about Technocrats that suggest that they can do what seems to be more or less mystical ( or technomagickal ) Magick Effects, as long as they do it in a scientific-seeming way - or at least a way that calls upon science tropes as seen by mundane humans. Going by this, it would be possible for an Iteration-X Technocrat to for example quickly create some explosives from materials that just happen to have properties &quot; overlooked by mundane scientists, but clearly apparent to the Technocrat Mage &quot; . Or do something else, along these lines. Like having a Correspondence 1 Magickal Sense without any device or machine, knowing exact distances due to a ' scientist's intuition ' that such a Technocrat has.<br /> Perhaps you could read the the Order of Reason book from Mage: Dark Ages in regards to ideas about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-05-2018, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T02:55:26-07:00","id":1215420,"title":"","content":"Recently, one of the more elusive procedures of Iteration X was recovered from the archives. Outdated now, it was in the realm of Masters at the time.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Program VCR (Mind 5, Forces 1, Data 1, Time 2)<br /> This procedure once allowed the masters of Technology to overcome a shortsightedness following the introduction of a certain a gadget to the masses: The Video Cassette Recorder. A fault in the coordination between Iteration X and the Syndicate, along with misplaced documentation, left a piece of the machine's technology in the realm of Enlightened Hypertech: Programming it to record on schedule.<br /> <br /> After the fallout and a re-adjusting of the Timetable, the NWO stepped in to aid Iteration X in the development of the procedure's crucial dependency on Data, as well as to make sure that contingencies among the masses were put into effect to mask up the Enlightened nature of the introduced technology.<br /> This near-vulgar Procedure was developed in order to salvage the mess and push the technology away from potential Market Correction.<br /> <br /> The core is a Mind 5 effect to push cognitive abilities beyond reasonable limits, as is temporarily necessary to handle the acts necessary to perform the programming. It gets combined with a sense of the flow of Data and an awareness of the effect of the resulting Forces inside the VCR's electronics to handle the exposed Hypertech components. This all gets combined with an application of subconcious read-ahead Time-Motion Sensititivity to guide the Mind into the right steps as to overcome the shortcomings of the official documentation.<br /> This allowed enlightened ( and somewhat degraded, given their status as Hypertech Masters.. ) 'service personell' covertly introduced in VCR Repair shops to successfully program the item according to the customer's wishes.<br /> <br /> A latter introduction of &quot;Revised documentation&quot; for the masses with this Procedure infused into the text as a subconcious effect triggered upon reading had an interesting consequence: The Procedure embedded into the written word seemingly had a chance to have near-Grimoire-like effects, pushing some minds close or towards Awakening.<br /> <br /> Claims that this Awakening almost always resulted in Marauderdom are officially treated as Reality Deviant propaganda by the NWO, however the existance of &quot;America's Funniest Home Videos&quot; is a historical fact that not even the NWO has been able to snuff out..<br /> <br /> <br /> ---","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-05-2018, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T10:09:17-07:00","id":1215541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1215237-iteration-x-procedures?p=1215405#post1215405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per the material written on the Technocracy and the Iteration-X Convention, they would need to prepare their Procedures in a machine shop or a laboratory beforehand. Building machines and devices, tuning machines and devices, recharging power, adjusting settings etc. Any tools and measurement devices would be created or modified in a laboratory or a machine shop beforehand. I think that this is within the Convention's Paradigm - their Inspired Science is so far ahead of what is most of the time possible in the world, that they cannot do their Effects without first doing all of their technocratic preparations and having the needed, specified tools and materials.<br /> <br /> I recall the revised Iteration-X Convention Book talking a lot about how the Iteration-X uses tools to accomplish their Magick - as per this, I think that free-form improvisation is discouraged, in favour of creating and preparing the right tools - machines, materials, devices - beforehand to be able to do a given Magickal Effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is a small amount of writings ( a Procedure here and there , and not much else that I know of ) about Technocrats that suggest that they can do what seems to be more or less mystical ( or technomagickal ) Magick Effects, as long as they do it in a scientific-seeming way - or at least a way that calls upon science tropes as seen by mundane humans. Going by this, it would be possible for an Iteration-X Technocrat to for example quickly create some explosives from materials that just happen to have properties overlooked by mundane scientists, but clearly apparent to the Technocrat Mage. Or do something else, along these lines. Like having a Correspondence 1 Magickal Sense without any device or machine, knowing exact distances due to a ' scientist's intuition ' that a Technocrat has.<br /> Perhaps you could read the the Order of Reason book from Mage: Dark Ages in regards to ideas about this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ill have to check out Dark Ages, thanks for the recommendation. I always want my characters to be able to thrive in any situation so I look into how my technocrats can thrive in a situation where they are lacking wonders or advanced tech. A lot of contingency seems to come from whether a technocrat can create effects with jury rigged effects from supplies they find, and I always thought it should be possible because its certainly not outside the realm of possibility for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16848-brassfist","name":"Brassfist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T15:17:20-07:00","id":1215605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1215237-iteration-x-procedures?p=1215420#post1215420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Recently, one of the more elusive procedures of Iteration X was recovered from the archives. Outdated now, it was in the realm of Masters at the time.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Program VCR (Mind 5, Forces 1, Data 1, Time 2)<br /> <br /> The core is a Mind 5 effect to push cognitive abilities beyond reasonable limits, as is temporarily necessary to handle the acts necessary to perform the programming.<br /> <br /> ---</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind 5 ???<br /> Isn't that overkill?<br /> <br /> I could give the VCR a mind of its own with mind 5 .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T15:24:56-07:00","id":1215607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RandyRando</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1215237-iteration-x-procedures?p=1215605#post1215605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 5 ???<br /> Isn't that overkill?<br /> <br /> I could give the VCR a mind of its own with mind 5 .</div> </div> </div> </div>It's required to push your mental abilities to the superhuman levels necessary!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"A